  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 permits sales of models failing above 5% to continue up to an 8% failure rate for an open-ended, regulator-set corrective period, while exact per-model results go to buyers and regulators but not the public, which favours Northwind's flagship. S5 keeps a mandatory 8-per-100,000 recall with no interim relief and explicitly rules out a permanent market ban, while S4 sets built-in suppression at 36 months, which favours Halcyon's cost position and is at the outer edge of acceptable."
